# Shell scripts and the Containerfile are executed inside a Linux container.
# Checked out with CRLF on Windows, the shebang line ends in \r and the build
# dies with "exit code: 126", which reads as a permissions problem and is not
# one. Cost me a rebuild; pinning LF so it cannot happen on a fresh clone.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Containerfile   text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
